  "reason": "The records collectively identify several relevant ingredients: temperature-dependent behavior in compositionally similar HEAs, potentially non-sluggish elemental diffusion, surface or interfacial energy effects, segregation, and the possibility that HEA behavior is governed by ordinary kinetic or thermodynamic mechanisms rather than entropy stabilization. However, none describes in situ vacuum heating of sub-10-nm noble-metal HEA nanoparticles or connects surface-energy-driven Au/Cu segregation with shape evolution, enhanced local diffusion, evaporation, and loss of small particles. Thus the literature points in the general direction, but reconstructing the specific experiment and coupled nanoparticle mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
